 "question": "Summarize the key differences between evaluation protocol v1 and v2.",
 "answer": "Evaluation Protocol v2 supersedes v1 for all projects starting in 2025. [S1] Key differences include: - v2 splits data 70% training, 15% validation, 15% test [S1]. - v2 uses k=5 cross-validation for mean and standard deviation of fold scores [S1]. - v2 sets random_state=42 everywhere [S1]. - v2's primary metric is F1 for imbalanced data, accuracy otherwise [S1]. - v1 is superseded by v2 for projects starting in 2025 [S2] [S3].",
